    "### Results of Data cleaning"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f6edda5e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "The preprocessing pipeline reduced the dataset from 6,210 to 5,527 reviews, resulting in the removal of 683 observations.\n",
    "The majority of removals occurred during the filtering of reviews containing unusually long tokens (reduced to 5,713 reviews) and repeated consecutive words (further reduced to 5,528 reviews). The basic text normalization step did not affect the dataset size, as it only transformed the text without removing observations. A small number of additional reviews were removed after becoming empty following the cleaning process, resulting in a final dataset of 5,527 reviews. This confirms that applying text normalization before removing empty reviews was necessary to ensure that all non-informative observations were properly identified.\n",
    "Overall, the cleaning process reduced noise and improved data consistency, making the dataset more suitable for subsequent machine learning models."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0f5a215b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Feature filtering"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8b9744e1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Feature filtering involves selecting relevant variables for the model and removing those that do not contribute meaningful information. This helps reduce noise and improves model performance. It is an important step in the machine learning pipeline, as retaining only the most relevant features allows the model to generalize better, train more efficiently, and become easier to interpret. In this study, irrelevant features such as identifiers and non-textual variables were removed to ensure that the model focuses on the review content.\n",
    "\n",
    "The review_id column was removed, as it serves only as a unique identifier and does not contain any meaningful information for the prediction task. Including such variables may introduce noise and increase the risk of overfitting, as the model could learn patterns that do not generalize.\n",
    "The review_date variable was excluded, as the task focuses on text-based classification rather than temporal patterns. This is further supported by the exploratory analysis, where time-related features (e.g., review hour) showed little correlation with the target variable, indicating limited predictive value.\n",
    "The helpful variable was also removed, as it reflects post-publication user feedback rather than the textual content of the review. The analysis showed that this variable is highly skewed, with most reviews receiving zero votes, and it exhibits little correlation with the rating. Including such a feature may introduce bias and is therefore not appropriate for this text-based classification task."
   ]
  },
