    "### Text representation\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "24191d95",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "After preprocessing and feature selection, the textual data must be converted into a numerical format in order to be used by machine learning models. In this study, TF-IDF was used to transform the review text into feature vectors, as it captures the importance of words relative to the dataset.\n",
    "In addition, both unigrams (single words) and bigrams (pairs of words) were included to capture contextual information. This is particularly useful in sentiment analysis, where phrases such as “not good” carry a different meaning than individual words."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "6d50b7ec",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#TD-IDF for all models, the model uses both single (unigrams) words and pairs (biggrams) of words.\n",
    "vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(\n",
    "    max_features=5000,\n",
    "    ngram_range=(1,2),\n",
    "    stop_words='english'\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b6cbe136",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "A maximum of 5000 features was used to limit the dimensionality of the data while retaining the most informative terms. English stop words were removed to eliminate common words that do not contribute meaningful information to the model."
   ]
